# .cursorrules — Cutting Edge v2 (thin pointer; the content lives in the linked files)

Read, in this order, before generating anything:
1. AGENTS.md — what this project is, the locked stack, how to build/test, the mandatory loop.
2. DESIGN.md — the only visual reference (tokens are machine-checked: `node scripts/check-design-tokens.js`).
3. docs/loop/00_INDEX.md — the numbered delivery loop; every change belongs to a step `S-xxx` with a CONTRACT.

Rules that are enforced by tooling, not taste:
- Stack is locked (see AGENTS.md §1). Do not add libraries outside it; supervisor check C15 fails the audit.
- UI only from DESIGN.md tokens; after UI work run `python scripts/design_audit.py apps/desktop/src --strict`.
- Never `transition: all`, never `outline-none` without a `focus-visible:` ring, never `div onClick` — use `<button>`.
- Dates/numbers through `Intl.*`; Persian-first RTL with logical CSS properties.
- Tests are real (FFmpeg-generated media, live server, Playwright DOM); never weaken a test to pass.
